            <ArticleTitle>A novel approach for assessing catheter position after ultrasound-guided placement of continuous interscalene block.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1015-6, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1213/ane.0b013e318161528a</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The increasing use of ultrasound has allowed anesthesiologists to perform nerve blocks with a high success rate and without nerve stimulation or eliciting a paresthesia. The ability to visualize peripheral nerve catheters using ultrasound is limited. We present a novel method to confirm the position of an interscalene catheter tip using injection of agitated contrast. The described technique is simple and allows timely assessment of catheter tip position.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
